WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320 line:78% align:center
I'm an aviation maintenance technician,
which basically means I help keep

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.610 line:78% align:center
airplanes safe and ready to fly.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.930 line:78% align:center
My team works on airplanes, checking
everything from the engines, wings,

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.550 line:78% align:center
and wheels to make sure
everything works properly.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.080 line:78% align:center
We're hands-on every day using tools,
inspecting parts, and fixing things

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.090 line:78% align:center
inside and outside the aircraft.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.590 line:78% align:center
To become an aviation maintenance
technician, you need an A&P license,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.320 line:78% align:center
airframe, and power plant, which you can
earn through a two-year aviation

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.750 line:78% align:center
or technical school program.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.860 line:78% align:center
If you are in school, focus on math,
physics, and basic engineering.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.740 line:78% align:center
These subjects are important
in the AMT world.
